        {
          "datasource": {
            "type": "motherduck-duckdb-datasource",
            "uid": "duckdb"
          },
          "format": 1,
          "rawQuery": true,
          "rawSql": "-- NOAA GFS 10 m wind, sea-level pressure and rain for the next two days in ONE\n-- request: 17 three-hourly steps of 53 x 51 = 2,703 cells, 45,951 rows.\n--\n-- Every other cell of the 0.5 degree archive, so one per degree -- a regular\n-- lattice, which the velocity layers need: they deduce the spacing from the\n-- coordinates and draw nothing if it wobbles.\n--\n-- Every step comes back, each row with its time, and the map's clock -- the bar\n-- at the bottom -- chooses which one is drawn: the latest inside its window.\n-- The dashboard's range, now-90m to now+90m, is that window when the map opens,\n-- so the step on show is the one nearest to now.\n--\n-- The request starts at the step at or before now - 90 minutes, so the window\n-- lies wholly inside the data. Started any later, kepler would clip the\n-- window's leading edge to the first step and leave it narrower than the three\n-- hours between steps, and a window that narrow, playing, spends stretches with\n-- no step inside it and draws nothing.\n--\n-- The window is written into the URL from `now()` itself, not from a variable:\n-- it stays the same URL for three hours, so ERDDAP answers every visitor after\n-- the first from its own cache, and no hidden variable rides along in shared\n-- links. `{0}` and `{1}` are `format`'s, not Grafana's.\n--\n-- `.csv0` has no header and no units row, so read_csv names by position. Only\n-- `[` and `]` need escaping (%5B/%5D). The four subscripts must be written\n-- identically or ERDDAP answers 400.\n--\n-- The wait is ERDDAP's and DuckDB's together. ERDDAP's cost grows with every\n-- variable: u and v alone take about 7 s, these four 18 to 25 s. And DuckDB\n-- sends a HEAD before the GET, for which ERDDAP builds the whole response too.\n-- `SET force_download` would halve it, but it outlives this query on a\n-- connection every dashboard shares, and would stop range requests into large\n-- Parquet elsewhere; `http_get` cannot send this URL at all -- it rewrites the\n-- query string, and ERDDAP answers 400.\nSELECT column0         AS time,\n       column1         AS latitude,\n       column2 - 360   AS longitude,\n       column3         AS u,\n       column4         AS v,\n       column5 / 100   AS pressure_hpa,  -- Pa\n       -- The same pressure a hundred thousand times over, for the isobars only:\n       -- the layer takes its slope per metre, so this one's reads in hPa per\n       -- 100 km, the unit its legend then shows.\n       column5 * 1000  AS isobar_field,\n       column6 * 3600  AS rain_mm_h,     -- kg m-2 s-1, a millimetre of water per square metre\n       -- What the dots are sized by. Capped, so the rare cloudburst does not set\n       -- the scale and shrink ordinary rain to specks.\n       least(column6 * 3600, 10) AS rain_mm_h_capped\nFROM read_csv(\n  format('https://pae-paha.pacioos.hawaii.edu/erddap/griddap/ncep_global.csv0?ugrd10m%5B({0}):1:({1})%5D%5B(-40.0):2:(12.0)%5D%5B(260.0):2:(310.0)%5D,vgrd10m%5B({0}):1:({1})%5D%5B(-40.0):2:(12.0)%5D%5B(260.0):2:(310.0)%5D,prmslmsl%5B({0}):1:({1})%5D%5B(-40.0):2:(12.0)%5D%5B(260.0):2:(310.0)%5D,pratesfc%5B({0}):1:({1})%5D%5B(-40.0):2:(12.0)%5D%5B(260.0):2:(310.0)%5D',\n    strftime(time_bucket(INTERVAL 3 HOUR, (now() AT TIME ZONE 'UTC') - INTERVAL 90 MINUTE),\n             '%Y-%m-%dT%H:%M:%SZ'),\n    strftime(time_bucket(INTERVAL 3 HOUR, (now() AT TIME ZONE 'UTC') - INTERVAL 90 MINUTE) + INTERVAL 48 HOUR,\n             '%Y-%m-%dT%H:%M:%SZ')),\n  header = false,\n  columns = {'column0': 'TIMESTAMP', 'column1': 'DOUBLE', 'column2': 'DOUBLE', 'column3': 'DOUBLE',\n             'column4': 'DOUBLE', 'column5': 'DOUBLE', 'column6': 'DOUBLE'},\n  nullstr = 'NaN')\nWHERE column3 IS NOT NULL AND column4 IS NOT NULL AND column5 IS NOT NULL\n",
          "refId": "A"
        }
      ],
      "title": "Pressure and wind: the synoptic chart",
      "type": "ubica-keplergl-panel"
    },
    {
